      "The bidisc log-log maximum is psh, has integrable exponential at every weight and trivial ambient ideals, while its genuine restriction has a logarithmic pole. It is a retained SGPT local example.",
      "On a curve finite restricted ideal zeros give finite atomic D_m. Stokes and finite-subset limits bound total trace atomic mass by the restricted background area, even if that area is zero.",
      "The uniformly integrable nonpositive Green kernel gives an L1 potential with precisely the atomic Lelong data; a smooth zero-integral Poisson correction gives a positive current in the original restricted background.",
      "Removing the pole set removes every atomic mass and no smooth residual mass. Changing admissible smooth backgrounds or probability forms changes the Green representative smoothly, hence preserves ordinary type.",
